  "reflectionText": "Habakkuk stood at his watch and looked out over the lean year that was coming, when the fig tree would not flourish and the flocks would be cut off from the fold. He lifted his voice and sang: yet I will rejoice in the Lord. What is the weariness of singing a song of joy in advance, for the year you can already see will not yield?"
